  "id": "ftya3h3",
  "title": "Chapter 29: Structure of the Earth",
  "order": 30,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cckn4zh",
      "content": "The Earth is made up of several concentric layers that differ in composition, density, temperature and physical state. Knowledge about the internal structure of the Earth is important for understanding earthquakes, volcanoes, plate tectonics and the formation of landforms."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
