            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mohorovicic Discontinuity (Moho)</p>",
            "<p>Between crust and mantle</p>",
            "<p>Sharp change in seismic wave velocity</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gutenberg Discontinuity</p>",
            "<p>Between mantle and core</p>",
            "<p>Separates mantle from liquid outer core</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lehmann Discontinuity</p>",
            "<p>Between outer core and inner core</p>",
            "<p>Separates liquid and solid core</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c90a5d8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xkamqo9",
      "content": "• Earth's radius is approximately 6371 km."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8x3i9gb",
      "content": "• Mantle is the thickest layer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h5qc38k",
      "content": "• Outer core is liquid and inner core is solid."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5lqpd9z",
      "content": "• Moho discontinuity separates crust and mantle."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}